(8412: (meta: (t: semantic) (n: 1) (term: string%20value) (def: Five%20complete%20source%20identities%20serve%20only%20the%20frozen%20raw%20consuming%20artifact%20and%20its%20historical%20consumers.%20Three%20original%20source%20certificates%20are%20projected%20automatically%20from%20existing%20archives%3B%20only%20the%20missing%20consuming%20host%20and%20checker%20are%20captured%20once.%20Complete%20stored%20source%20certificates%20make%20later%20freshness%20independent%20of%20those%20archives.%20The%20current%20producer%20retains%20its%20physical%20source%20metadata%20separately%20and%20must%20reproduce%20every%20complete%20original%20semantic%20artifact%20field%20and%20both%20codecs%20before%20snapshot%20comparison.%20Source%20conservation%20is%20not%20general%20semantic%20equivalence%20or%20native%20execution%20evidence.) (lang: meta-language%20structured%20data)))
